                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0964961-b4f8-3771-af52-73c1f3b3453d",
                        "entry_id": "d447a95c-39ee-3635-84cf-22c39d0fae3e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Féminin singulier de révélateur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2002719e-f3b7-4bfb-bdc8-3009f4406fbf",
                                "sense_id": "d0964961-b4f8-3771-af52-73c1f3b3453d",
                                "text": "C'est alors que l’ivraie et le bon grain, le mal et le bien, si mystérieusement entremêlés ici-bas, vont tenter de se désécheveler, de se dégager l’un de l'autre, de se présenter dans leur nudité révélatrice, pour conquérir la terre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "498f518d-50a9-3607-9007-67abf9c1d452",
                "word": "révélatrice",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "711c4252-5e1b-4afd-96b3-679993cc13d9",
                        "entry_id": "498f518d-50a9-3607-9007-67abf9c1d452",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "révélatrices"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "7fb5cca4-8cc1-462c-a113-a35dd216e40f",
                        "entry_id": "498f518d-50a9-3607-9007-67abf9c1d452",
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "form": "révélateur"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eef2fce1-5167-30ec-89a9-25172ad074b1",
                        "entry_id": "498f518d-50a9-3607-9007-67abf9c1d452",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celle qui fait la révélation d’un complot politique de quelque association criminelle, de quelque affaire secrète."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d23e2c54-1d62-4820-874e-07e72352d12e",
                                "sense_id": "eef2fce1-5167-30ec-89a9-25172ad074b1",
                                "text": "Le destin a refusé à Marie Lenéru la parole ; elle se surmonte et d’une insuffisance tire une supériorité. Elle sera la révélatrice qui nous apporte le message de la plus profonde solitude."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a03ad067-dcab-3327-a4e8-932a19e1700f",
                        "entry_id": "498f518d-50a9-3607-9007-67abf9c1d452",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ce qui permet la révélation d’un phénomène ignoré."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "analogy"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "58050898-4177-4e6d-858e-af5238db81ac",
                                "sense_id": "a03ad067-dcab-3327-a4e8-932a19e1700f",
                                "text": "Toute la question est maintenant de savoir si cette activité peut devenir la révélatrice de l’intelligence ; en autres termes, si les faits que l’homme produit sous la seule instigation de son instinct peuvent devenir des signes pour son esprit, de telle manière qu’il soit tout à la fois, de lui-même à lui-même, par l’appel de sa spontanéité et la réponse de son intelligence, initiateur et initié ?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "59929718-d877-4cfa-9bcd-a58e80f81ec5",
                        "source_entry_id": "498f518d-50a9-3607-9007-67abf9c1d452",
                        "target_lang_word": "revealer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "revealer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4da921f9-28a4-3ed7-a484-0805c0892e98",
                                        "entry_id": "de6ca9d4-7426-3785-a38f-e66857c6f22c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or thing that reveals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1b84279-043a-4b8c-a71a-415c719ee06f",
                                                "sense_id": "4da921f9-28a4-3ed7-a484-0805c0892e98",
                                                "text": "Whether \"The Doctor\" be written by Southey or not, let revealers of mysteries determine; it is certainly written by one who strongly resembles him, perhaps too strongly to be other than himself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23ea18ef-d03f-325d-8ecf-662439a2e9b8",
                                        "entry_id": "de6ca9d4-7426-3785-a38f-e66857c6f22c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An entry in a crossword that guides the solver towards the theme or endgame."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8dfe8ae-a64c-4487-8100-335fc4661d35",
                                                "sense_id": "23ea18ef-d03f-325d-8ecf-662439a2e9b8",
                                                "text": "Next (and my favorite) is Blank Space , four corner rebus squares reading \"blank\" for the down answers and \"space\" for the acrosses, mirroring the central revealers"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db256b52-8629-4805-86d4-f9a05c7b3596",
                                                "sense_id": "23ea18ef-d03f-325d-8ecf-662439a2e9b8",
                                                "text": "Though experienced solvers will likely see where this is going , others might need the help of the revealer"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12cd0857-29ce-45ce-9714-bbdba1dee695",
                                                "sense_id": "23ea18ef-d03f-325d-8ecf-662439a2e9b8",
                                                "text": "The theme launches off a main revealer entry at 93-Across. There are four clues that refer to that entry, at 39-, 65-, 104- and 108-Across. When solved, 93-Across will also make the grid art snap into focus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cd90b78b-526b-43e7-a3a7-0fecd85b9e1e",
                        "source_entry_id": "498f518d-50a9-3607-9007-67abf9c1d452",
                        "target_lang_word": "revelator",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "revelator",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b102aef-6863-3db6-ae2a-c4b22d9e9666",
                                        "entry_id": "049d3411-2d75-30be-9c00-ef1bc318df66",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or personified agent who reveals; especially, one who makes a divine revelation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18d40d13-4fe8-4383-9145-5221af65cb5a",
                                                "sense_id": "5b102aef-6863-3db6-ae2a-c4b22d9e9666",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: revealer; discloser, divulger; uncoverer, unveiler; discoverer; clairvoyant, seer, prophet"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77cab2f1-fd45-447f-a119-0dbbd5cb6be8",
                                                "sense_id": "5b102aef-6863-3db6-ae2a-c4b22d9e9666",
                                                "text": "But it was Paul to whom the Lord revealed the whole doctrine of the mystery; and we firmly believe he thus became the revelator to all men of these glorious things connected with this mystery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cfbe715-9700-4fa6-bbbb-15d57f0be808",
                                                "sense_id": "5b102aef-6863-3db6-ae2a-c4b22d9e9666",
                                                "text": "We noted in earlier chapters that the Twelve, beginning in Joseph Smith's day, were sustained as prophets, seers, and revelators, and that the Quorum of the Twelve were sustained as the First Presidency of the Church following the death of Brigham Young."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36ff4749-067e-4183-a35c-e5c1503ef5c4",
                                                "sense_id": "5b102aef-6863-3db6-ae2a-c4b22d9e9666",
                                                "text": "They caught the Katy\nAnd left me a mule to ride\nThe fortune lady\nCame along, she walked beside\nBut every word seemed to date her\nTime's the revelator\nThe revelator\n[…]\nQueen of fakes and imitators\nTime's the revelator"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bda01815-74d4-4c6d-a43f-f5269777e919",
                                                "sense_id": "5b102aef-6863-3db6-ae2a-c4b22d9e9666",
                                                "text": "Alvin Toffler or George Gilder might have been more likely choices for back-page revelators, but Negroponte ponied up $75,000 in seed money when the Old Media barons were showing Wired founders Louis Rossetto and Jane Metcalfe the door."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e45a65e-e9e2-43c3-a287-18106b3389a1",
                                                "sense_id": "5b102aef-6863-3db6-ae2a-c4b22d9e9666",
                                                "text": "A Revelator song notable for its classic uses of balance and incremental repetition, for its fusion of New Testament apocalyptic images, its folk diction and syntax fitted out as pulpit rhetoric and prophecy, and its sensitivity to simultaneously occurring dimensions of time and space.\nThe vision of the speaker, superimposed on the apocalyptic vision of John the Revelator, includes all time and eternity: the remote past during which the Revelator, from exile on Patmos, wrote his letters to the seven churches; the immediate past of the dead mother who now dwells on the island with the prophet; the present of the \"leader\" or preacher who, as head of the church to which the speaker belongs, has received a \"letter\"—the Book of Revelation itself—from John; the eternal present in which the speaker and the prophet coexist spiritually; and the rapidly approaching future, the last days which John prophesied."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
